; SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 MAINLINE contributors
; SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
;
; SEVEN CONTRACTS, and TWENTY-NINE ROOT PACKAGES. Both numbers moved on 2026-08-10 and
; each move closed a measured hole rather than adding a rule.
;
; THE HOLE IN `root_packages`. This file used to name FIVE root packages against
; TWENTY-SEVEN distributions on disk. Import-linter builds a real import graph over its
; roots and over nothing else, so the other twenty-two packages were not being linted by
; ANY contract — including `trappoint-core`, which holds the retry loop contract 4 exists
; to protect. The registry mechanism described below is what was supposed to prevent
; that; it is now implemented, in `scripts/qa/check_import_registry.py`, and it refuses a
; build when a distribution appears in neither `root_packages` nor a contract's
; `forbidden_modules`.
;
; WHY EACH CONTRACT EXISTS. Each one exists because a claim made elsewhere in this
; repository is false without it:
;
;   1. licence-boundary   — "the substrate is Apache-2.0 and forkable" is a lie the
;                           moment an Apache distribution imports an FSL one, because
;                           the fork cannot then be built.
;   2. no-model-in-kernel — ARCHITECTURE.md §8.2 draws the deterministic boundary and
;                           `mainline-boundary`'s E3 enforcement asserts it over the
;                           dependency graph. This contract asserts the same thing over
;                           the IMPORT graph, which is the surface E3 cannot see.
;   3. verifier-minimal   — `trappoint-verify`'s whole value is that an opposing expert
;                           can run it with one dependency. Every import added to the
;                           canonicalisation path is a dependency their Rust
;                           re-implementation would have to reproduce.
;   4. no-blanket-retry   — spec/errors.md §4: a refusal is attempted exactly once,
;                           ever. `tenacity`/`backoff`/`retrying` make the retry policy
;                           a decorator argument nobody reads, and a retried `23514`
;                           turns the refusal ledger's count into a count of nothing.
;   5. gate-service-model-free — the loudest security claim in the product ("no model can
;                           reach the merge gate") was, until 2026-08-10, a contract
;                           forbidding the import of a package nobody had written. The
;                           package exists now, so the claim is falsifiable.
;   6. testkit-forkable   — the substrate testkit must survive a fork that keeps
;                           `packages/` and deletes `verticals/`. Contract 1 forbids the
;                           FSL vertical; this one also forbids the Apache-but-MAINLINE
;                           packages, which contract 1 cannot reach because they are not
;                           FSL.
;   7. verifier-offline   — contract 3 makes the promise about `trappoint-jcs`. This one
;                           makes it about `trappoint-verify`, which is the artefact the
;                           promise is actually about: the offline verifier a court's
;                           expert runs on a machine with no cluster and no network.
;
; HOW A NEW PACKAGE JOINS. `root_packages` must name packages that are importable at
; lint time — import-linter builds a real graph, not a guess, and a name that resolves to
; nothing fails the whole run with `Could not find package '…' in your Python path`
; (measured). So a package that does not exist yet cannot be listed. The mechanism that
; stops that from becoming a hole is `scripts/qa/check_import_registry.py`, run by the
; `import-linter-registry` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: it fails when a workspace
; distribution appears in neither `root_packages` (its imports are checked) nor a
; contract's `forbidden_modules` (importing it is checked). A new package is registered
; by CI refusing the build, not by anyone remembering.
;
; `mainline_corpus` is deliberately NOT a root package: `verticals/mainline/packages/
; mainline-corpus/` has source but no `pyproject.toml`, so it is not an installable
; distribution and not importable at lint time. It is registered through contract 1's
; `forbidden_modules`, and it joins `root_packages` in the same commit that gives it a
; `pyproject.toml`.

[importlinter]
root_packages =
    mainline_agentkit
    mainline_anchor
    mainline_archivist
    mainline_boundary
    mainline_cartographer
    mainline_cherrypick
    mainline_custody_patrol
    mainline_delta_oracle
    mainline_domain
    mainline_fixity
    mainline_gate_svc
    mainline_mcp
    mainline_mutation
    mainline_quarantine
    mainline_recall_agent
    mainline_recall_fleet
    mainline_sequencer
    mainline_steward
    trappoint_conformance
    trappoint_core
    trappoint_diagnose
    trappoint_jcs
    trappoint_ledger
    trappoint_migrate
    trappoint_model
    trappoint_recall
    trappoint_sql
    trappoint_testkit
    trappoint_verify
include_external_packages = True
exclude_type_checking_imports = False

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; CONTRACT 1 — the Apache substrate never imports the FSL vertical.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Direction matters and only one direction is forbidden. `verticals/mainline/*` MAY
; import `packages/trappoint-*`: that is the substrate claim working. The reverse makes
; `packages/` unbuildable outside this repository, which is the entire fork story.
;
; Forbidden entries that do not exist yet are skipped by import-linter rather than
; erroring, so this list is written for the whole vertical up front and the contract
; starts enforcing each package the day it lands.
;
; 2026-08-10: `source_modules` was FIVE names against fourteen Apache distributions, so
; the sentence in this heading was true of a third of the substrate. It now names every
; distribution under `packages/`. Measured before widening — no `packages/*/src` file
; imports any `mainline_*` vertical module, directly or indirectly — so this is a
; widening of the assertion, not a change to the code.
[importlinter:contract:licence-boundary]
name = 1. The Apache substrate never imports the FSL vertical
type = forbidden
source_modules =
    mainline_agentkit
    mainline_boundary
    mainline_mcp
    trappoint_conformance
    trappoint_core
    trappoint_diagnose
    trappoint_jcs
    trappoint_ledger
    trappoint_migrate
    trappoint_model
    trappoint_recall
    trappoint_sql
    trappoint_testkit
    trappoint_verify
forbidden_modules =
    mainline_anchor
    mainline_archivist
    mainline_cartographer
    mainline_cherrypick
    mainline_console_api
    mainline_corpus
    mainline_custody_patrol
    mainline_custody_relay
    mainline_delta_oracle
    mainline_domain
    mainline_fixity
    mainline_gate_svc
    mainline_ingest
    mainline_mutation
    mainline_provisioner
    mainline_quarantine
    mainline_recall_agent
    mainline_recall_fleet
    mainline_sequencer
    mainline_steward
allow_indirect_imports = False
unmatched_ignore_imports_alerting = error

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; CONTRACT 2 — no model code path in the kernel.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; The gate is deterministic SQL and the tools that apply and test it. If a model SDK is
; importable from the migration runner or the conformance runner, then "no model can
; reach the merge gate" is a claim about intent rather than about the program.
;
; `allow_indirect_imports = False` is the point: a transitive reach through a helper
; module is the shape this actually takes in practice, never a direct `import boto3`
; at the top of `runner.py`.
;
; 2026-08-10: widened from `trappoint_migrate` + `trappoint_conformance` to every
; `packages/trappoint-*` distribution, which is the root set ARCHITECTURE.md §8.2 E3
; actually names (`mainline_boundary.astscan.DEFAULT_KERNEL_ROOTS`). `trappoint_core`
; holds the gate transaction itself and was not covered by this contract until today.
; `mainline_boundary` and `mainline_agentkit` are deliberately NOT sources: both import
; `boto3` on purpose — the first to interrogate IAM, the second because it IS the model
; client — and both live outside the kernel plane for exactly that reason.
[importlinter:contract:no-model-in-kernel]
name = 2. No model code path in the kernel (every packages/trappoint-*)
type = forbidden
source_modules =
    trappoint_conformance
    trappoint_core
    trappoint_diagnose
    trappoint_jcs
    trappoint_ledger
    trappoint_migrate
    trappoint_model
    trappoint_recall
    trappoint_sql
    trappoint_testkit
    trappoint_verify
forbidden_modules =
    boto3
    botocore
    anthropic
    strands
    strands_agents
    strands_tools
    openai
    langchain
    langchain_core
    llama_index
    transformers
    sentence_transformers
    torch
    mainline_agentkit
allow_indirect_imports = False
unmatched_ignore_imports_alerting = error

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; CONTRACT 3 — the offline verifier's canonicaliser stays dependency-minimal.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; `trappoint-jcs` is the canonicaliser the offline verifier vendors, and its
; `pyproject.toml` declares zero runtime dependencies. That declaration is a promise
; about the DISTRIBUTION; this contract is the promise about the CODE, which is the one
; that breaks first — a single `import numpy` inside a canonicalisation helper survives
; a dependency-list review and then appears in the verifier's install footprint.
;
; `trappoint_verify` now exists, and it gets its OWN contract (7) rather than joining
; this one: the two artefacts fail differently and a merged contract would report one
; line where an auditor needs two.
[importlinter:contract:verifier-minimal]
name = 3. The offline verifier's canonicaliser stays dependency-minimal
type = forbidden
source_modules =
    trappoint_jcs
forbidden_modules =
    psycopg
    psycopg_pool
    boto3
    botocore
    requests
    httpx
    urllib3
    aiohttp
    numpy
    scipy
    pandas
    sklearn
    pydantic
    jinja2
    yaml
    anthropic
allow_indirect_imports = False
unmatched_ignore_imports_alerting = error

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; CONTRACT 4 — no blanket-retry helper exists anywhere.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Repository-wide, including the FSL vertical and the evaluation harness. `40001` is the
; only retryable SQLSTATE (spec/errors.md §2.1) and the loop that retries it is
; hand-written, bounded, jittered and readable in one screen. A decorator that retries
; "on exception" cannot distinguish an undecided transaction from a decided refusal, and
; the difference between those two is the product.
;
; 2026-08-10: "anywhere" now means anywhere. `source_modules` was five names; it is now
; every root package. Measured before widening — no `src` file in any distribution
; imports `tenacity`, `backoff`, `retrying`, `stamina` or a relative — so this widening
; records a property the repository already had and refuses its loss.
[importlinter:contract:no-blanket-retry]
name = 4. No blanket-retry helper exists anywhere
type = forbidden
source_modules =
    mainline_agentkit
    mainline_anchor
    mainline_archivist
    mainline_boundary
    mainline_cartographer
    mainline_cherrypick
    mainline_custody_patrol
    mainline_delta_oracle
    mainline_domain
    mainline_fixity
    mainline_gate_svc
    mainline_mcp
    mainline_mutation
    mainline_quarantine
    mainline_recall_agent
    mainline_recall_fleet
    mainline_sequencer
    mainline_steward
    trappoint_conformance
    trappoint_core
    trappoint_diagnose
    trappoint_jcs
    trappoint_ledger
    trappoint_migrate
    trappoint_model
    trappoint_recall
    trappoint_sql
    trappoint_testkit
    trappoint_verify
forbidden_modules =
    tenacity
    backoff
    retrying
    retry
    retry2
    stamina
    aiohttp_retry
allow_indirect_imports = False
unmatched_ignore_imports_alerting = error

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; CONTRACT 5 — the gate service cannot reach a model. This is THE claim.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; `mainline-gate-svc` is the only process that calls `mainline.merge_permit`. Everything
; the product says about determinism reduces to a statement about this one distribution's
; closure, and until 2026-08-10 that statement was unfalsifiable: contract 1 forbade
; importing `mainline_gate_svc`, `boundary.yml` triggered on its path, and E3 scanned it
; — and the package did not exist. A scan over an absent path finds nothing, and
; `mainline_boundary.astscan` was honest enough to record `E3-ROOT-ABSENT` as a skip
; rather than print that nothing as green.
;
; The package exists now. Its three runtime dependencies are `psycopg[binary]`,
; `trappoint-core` and `mainline-domain`; its own suite walks `sys.modules` after import
; AND walks `importlib.metadata.requires` transitively, because a runtime absence with a
; declared dependency is still a supply-chain reach.
;
; This contract is the third independent surface, over the IMPORT GRAPH, and it does not
; share a failure mode with either of the other two: deleting the test does not delete
; this, and deleting this does not delete the test.
;
; `allow_indirect_imports = False` is not decoration. The realistic shape of this failure
; is `mainline_gate_svc.report` importing a vertical helper that imports
; `mainline_agentkit` for one convenience function.
[importlinter:contract:gate-service-model-free]
name = 5. The merge-gate service can reach no model SDK, directly or transitively
type = forbidden
source_modules =
    mainline_gate_svc
forbidden_modules =
    boto3
    botocore
    anthropic
    anthropic_bedrock
    claude_agent_sdk
    strands
    strands_agents
    strands_tools
    openai
    langchain
    langchain_aws
    langchain_core
    langgraph
    litellm
    llama_index
    transformers
    sentence_transformers
    torch
    instructor
    mainline_agentkit
    mainline_delta_oracle
allow_indirect_imports = False
unmatched_ignore_imports_alerting = error

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; CONTRACT 6 — the testkit is substrate, and substrate must survive a fork.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; `trappoint-testkit` is the harness a second vertical inherits: one cluster fixture,
; four DSN spellings, and the container discipline that stopped this repository's suite
; from starting thirteen CockroachDB nodes at once (quality-repair.md §1.4). A fork keeps
; `packages/` and deletes `verticals/`; a testkit that imports anything MAINLINE-shaped
; does not survive that deletion, and the fork's first `pytest` fails on an import error
; in the harness itself — the least diagnosable failure a stranger can meet.
;
; This is NOT contract 1 with a different name. Contract 1 forbids the FSL vertical.
; `mainline_boundary`, `mainline_agentkit` and `mainline_mcp` are Apache-2.0 and live
; under `packages/`, so contract 1 permits them — and every one of them is MAINLINE
; domain knowledge that a second vertical does not have and does not want.
[importlinter:contract:testkit-forkable]
name = 6. The substrate testkit imports nothing MAINLINE-shaped
type = forbidden
source_modules =
    trappoint_testkit
forbidden_modules =
    mainline_agentkit
    mainline_anchor
    mainline_archivist
    mainline_boundary
    mainline_cartographer
    mainline_cherrypick
    mainline_console_api
    mainline_corpus
    mainline_custody_patrol
    mainline_custody_relay
    mainline_delta_oracle
    mainline_domain
    mainline_fixity
    mainline_gate_svc
    mainline_ingest
    mainline_mcp
    mainline_mutation
    mainline_provisioner
    mainline_quarantine
    mainline_recall_agent
    mainline_recall_fleet
    mainline_sequencer
    mainline_steward
allow_indirect_imports = False
unmatched_ignore_imports_alerting = error

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; CONTRACT 7 — the offline verifier runs with no cluster and no network.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; `trappoint-verify` is the artefact VERIFY.md hands to an opposing expert: given an
; exported ledger segment and a signed root, it recomputes the tree and says yes or no,
; on a laptop, with no credential of ours and no machine of ours. That promise dies the
; instant the verifier needs a database driver or an HTTP client — not because the import
; is slow, but because it means the verification is no longer independent of the system
; being verified, and an independent verification that phones home has verified nothing.
;
; Measured 2026-08-10: `packages/trappoint-verify/src` imports `argparse`, `base64`,
; `binascii`, `contextlib`, `hashlib`, `json`, `math`, `os`, `sys` and the stdlib typing
; modules, and nothing else. This contract is what keeps that true.
;
; `psycopg` heads the list on purpose: it is the ONE dependency the rest of this
; repository takes for granted, which makes it the one that arrives here by accident.
[importlinter:contract:verifier-offline]
name = 7. The offline verifier imports no driver and no network client
type = forbidden
source_modules =
    trappoint_verify
forbidden_modules =
    psycopg
    psycopg_pool
    psycopg2
    asyncpg
    sqlalchemy
    requests
    httpx
    httpcore
    urllib3
    aiohttp
    websockets
    boto3
    botocore
    anthropic
    openai
    pydantic
    numpy
    pandas
allow_indirect_imports = False
unmatched_ignore_imports_alerting = error
